WEBVTT

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:11.269
<v Tomasz Nowak>Morning, everyone. Monday the twentieth. Can you hear me, or am I doing the Teams mime again?</v>

00:00:12.689 --> 00:00:19.339
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, you're there. Better than my weekend, anyway. Had plans for a barbecue and the weather absolutely did us.</v>

00:00:20.879 --> 00:00:25.079
<v David Whitfield>That's because you announced it. Never tell the British weather your intentions.</v>

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:32.079
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Next weekend's plans are indoors. Not falling for that little sunshine symbol again.</v>

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:40.079
<v Callum Reid>Talking of shiny things, whose new car is that in the car park? Very brave parking it under those trees.</v>

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:44.880
<v Sarah Okafor>Not mine. Mine's the one with more biscuit crumbs than upholstery.</v>

00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:49.369
<v Callum Reid>Ah, factory specification. Mine's got that package as well.</v>

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.420
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, before we get onto finance options. Finished bits first?</v>

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:01.390
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I already swapped the filter on the Stretch Wrapper yesterday. That's done.</v>

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:05.489
<v David Whitfield>Oh, right. I was looking at the old entry, then.</v>

00:01:06.819 --> 00:01:09.969
<v Priya Raman>You were, yeah. Nothing left on that filter change.</v>

00:01:10.719 --> 00:01:17.370
<v Callum Reid>And I signed off the inspection on the turbine one on Tuesday. Last Tuesday, obviously. That's finished as well.</v>

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:22.019
<v Tomasz Nowak>Lovely. Both historical, not more work for this morning.</v>

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:29.939
<v Aisha Begum>Just an observation from me: heard a slight rattle from the line 2 interlock. Nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:30.879 --> 00:01:35.430
<v David Whitfield>Just a little chatter, was it? Not calling for a job on it?</v>

00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:41.650
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly. A slight rattle, that's all I'm reporting. No action off the back of that yet.</v>

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:47.930
<v Tomasz Nowak>Separately, Sarah, can you check the guarding on the line 2 robot at half two?</v>

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:53.859
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll check the guarding on the line 2 robot at half two.</v>

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:00.319
<v Tomasz Nowak>Normal priority on that. It's not an escalation from the rattle observation.</v>

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:03.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Normal priority, half two.</v>

00:02:03.569 --> 00:02:10.569
<v Callum Reid>Before I forget, that charity bake sale on Friday was brilliant. Last Friday, I mean. Whoever did the lemon cake—</v>

00:02:11.439 --> 00:02:14.590
<v Olumide Adeyemi>—accounted for most of your lunch? Yeah, we noticed.</v>

00:02:16.189 --> 00:02:24.240
<v Tomasz Nowak>Back to machinery, cake-powered or otherwise. Callum, can you book a contractor to look at the wrapper? Monday for the booking, low priority.</v>

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:31.629
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll book a contractor to look at the wrapper Monday, so today. Low priority, understood.</v>

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:36.699
<v David Whitfield>That's the booking today, not expecting a contractor through the gate today?</v>

00:02:38.689 --> 00:02:43.590
<v Tomasz Nowak>Correct. Monday is for making the booking. We're not agreeing an arrival time here.</v>

00:02:44.229 --> 00:02:48.780
<v Callum Reid>Fine, I've got the booking. And that's separate from the finished filter change.</v>

00:02:50.199 --> 00:02:56.849
<v Priya Raman>While we're on suppliers, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the Main Water Isolation Valve. Still blocked.</v>

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.389
<v Aisha Begum>So that hasn't actually moved since the last update?</v>

00:03:02.639 --> 00:03:08.240
<v Priya Raman>No. No confirmed delivery. Just reporting the same blocker, not putting another job on today's list.</v>

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:11.199
<v Tomasz Nowak>Okay, that stays as a blocker.</v>

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:17.860
<v Tomasz Nowak>Saz, can you chase the purchase order for the forklifts today at 2pm? Normal priority.</v>

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:24.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, I'll chase the purchase order for the forklifts today at 2pm. Normal priority.</v>

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:30.580
<v Olumide Adeyemi>You've got the afternoon in nice little slices, haven't you?</v>

00:03:31.969 --> 00:03:36.520
<v Sarah Okafor>Apparently. Purchase order at two, guarding at half two. Different things, both clear.</v>

00:03:36.879 --> 00:03:42.830
<v Tomasz Nowak>Aisha, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve today at 2pm?</v>

00:03:44.939 --> 00:03:51.240
<v Aisha Begum>Sorry, no, I can't take that sign-off. I'm not available at two, so don't put that against me.</v>

00:03:53.479 --> 00:04:01.530
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, Callum, can you take that instead of Aisha: do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve today at 2pm?</v>

00:04:02.039 --> 00:04:09.039
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I can take it. I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve today at 2pm.</v>

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:14.759
<v David Whitfield>And the relief valve seals—those are a separate item from that sign-off, yeah?</v>

00:04:16.509 --> 00:04:21.410
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, separate items. Don't merge them just because both have valve in the name.</v>

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:27.509
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, I'll replace the seals on the relief valve today.</v>

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.120
<v Tomasz Nowak>Thanks, Olu. The relief valve seals are yours today, then.</v>

00:04:32.829 --> 00:04:34.579
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, I'll do those today.</v>

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:42.220
<v David Whitfield>Got you. That's the distinction I was after; the short names can sound the same over this audio.</v>

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:48.689
<v Tomasz Nowak>Cal, can you order spare parts for the palletizer as well? That's fairly important.</v>

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:54.089
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll order spare parts for the palletizer. Fairly important, got it.</v>

00:04:56.470 --> 00:05:01.370
<v Aisha Begum>Sorry, you clipped slightly. Was that the important one, rather than the contractor booking?</v>

00:05:02.509 --> 00:05:06.709
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yes. Spare parts for the palletizer: fairly important. Contractor booking: low priority.</v>

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:12.589
<v Callum Reid>That's how I've got them. Parts order is mine as well.</v>

00:05:14.959 --> 00:05:21.610
<v Callum Reid>One blocker before we finish: I can't get to the Fire Alarm Panel until production gives us a window.</v>

00:05:23.949 --> 00:05:29.899
<v Sarah Okafor>There isn't an agreed window at the moment. I can't give you a time on this call.</v>

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:36.329
<v Callum Reid>Right, so that stays parked. Not saying I'm doing the Fire Alarm Panel today.</v>

00:05:38.689 --> 00:05:40.439
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. Blocked, not another allocation.</v>

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:48.509
<v Priya Raman>Is anyone else getting every third word through a tin can, or is that just my headset?</v>

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:53.329
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Bit of both, I reckon. Teams has decided we're all underwater.</v>

00:05:55.600 --> 00:06:00.149
<v David Whitfield>There's quite a lot of background noise at my end. Probably not helping.</v>

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:06.300
<v Aisha Begum>The actual decisions came through, anyway. It was mostly the cake discussion that broke up.</v>

00:06:07.329 --> 00:06:12.930
<v Tomasz Nowak>Probably for the best. Everyone clear on what they've accepted, and what's just blocked or finished?</v>

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:15.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, all clear here.</v>

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:19.970
<v Callum Reid>Same here. No mystery jobs hiding in the cake chat.</v>

00:06:20.819 --> 00:06:22.920
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good. That's us, then. Cheers, everyone.</v>
